.TH FEGETENV 3 "2026-05-03" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
fegetenv, fesetenv \- get and set the floating-point environment
.SH LIBRARY
Math Library (libm, \-lm)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <fenv.h>
.PP
.BI "int fegetenv(fenv_t *" envp );
.BI "int fesetenv(const fenv_t *" envp );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR fegetenv ()
and
.BR fesetenv ()
functions save and restore the complete floating-point environment, which
includes the rounding mode, exception sticky flags, and (on x87) the
exception masks.
.SS fegetenv
.BR fegetenv ()
stores a snapshot of the current floating-point environment into the object
pointed to by
.IR envp .
.PP
On x87, this is implemented with the
.B fnstenv
instruction, which also has the side effect of masking all x87 exceptions in
the hardware control word.
.BR fegetenv ()
corrects this by immediately reloading the saved control word so that the
calling program's exception masks are left unchanged.
.PP
The value stored in
.IR *envp
is opaque; it must not be modified directly.
It may only be passed to
.BR fesetenv ()
or
.BR feupdateenv (3).
.SS fesetenv
.BR fesetenv ()
installs the floating-point environment from the object pointed to by
.IR envp .
This restores the rounding mode, exception flags, and exception masks to the
saved values.
.PP
.BR fesetenv ()
does
.I not
raise any floating-point exceptions (even if the restored sticky flags
include set exception bits).
Use
.BR feupdateenv (3)
if the saved exceptions should be re-raised.
.PP
The special constant
.B FE_DFL_ENV
may be passed as
.IR envp
to install the default floating-point environment: round-to-nearest, all
exception flags cleared, all exception traps masked.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Both functions return zero on success.
A non-zero return value indicates failure.
.SH ERRORS
No errors are defined.
Neither function sets
.IR errno .
.SH EXAMPLES
The following example saves the full environment, modifies the rounding mode
and clears the exception flags, performs a computation, and then restores the
original environment:
.PP
.nf
#pragma STDC FENV_ACCESS ON
#include <fenv.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void)
{
    fenv_t saved;

    /* Save the full floating-point environment. */
    fegetenv(&saved);

    /* Modify: switch to round-toward-zero and clear all exceptions. */
    fesetround(FE_TOWARDZERO);
    feclearexcept(FE_ALL_EXCEPT);

    volatile double x = 7.0 / 2.0;   /* 3.0 under FE_TOWARDZERO */
    printf("7.0 / 2.0 (FE_TOWARDZERO) = %g\\n", x);

    /* Restore original environment (does NOT re-raise any exceptions). */
    fesetenv(&saved);

    return 0;
}
.fi
.PP
To restore to the default environment:
.PP
.nf
fesetenv(FE_DFL_ENV);
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fenv (7),
.BR feholdexcept (3),
.BR feupdateenv (3),
.BR fegetround (3)
